TI  - Healthy cookies from cooked fish bones
T2  - FOOD BIOSCIENCE
AB  - Nile tilapia fish are a staple food fish in Egypt. The objective of this research was to enrich a flaxseed and cinnamon cookie with cooked Nile tilapia fish bones (NTF). NTF at 6%, 12%, 18% and 24% of the wheat flour was used to fortify the cookies. Proximate analysis, Ca, P, Fe, total omega 3 fatty acids, and physical and sensory evaluation of cookies were done. The incorporation of NTF increased the total ash, Ca, and P at 12% NTF and above. The panelists gave the best score (statistically significant at 13`0.05) to the 12% NTF cookies. The consumption of 100 g of the 12% enriched cookies provided 39%, 34%, 62%, and 57% of the US RDA for females over 50 yr of protein, Ca, P, and Fe, respectively, along with 238% of the omega 3 fatty acids recommended by American Heart Association for those having cardiovascular disease. (C) 2015 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.
