TI  - Influence of Temperature Regime in Gas Chromatography on Polyunsaturated Fatty Acid Determination in <i>Petrovskaklobasa</i>
T2  - ROMANIAN BIOTECHNOLOGICAL LETTERS
AB  - Multi-linear programming, known also as step programming, was applied in order to optimize chromatographic parameters and provide the best separation of fatty acid in food samples. After achieving the best parameters, obtained method was applied to compare different methods of FAMEs preparation which were performed to Petrovskaklobasa as a matrix. It was noticed that in situ method provided good results compared to method based on extraction procedure, and therefore in situ method can be used for commercial purposes, since reduces the duration of the analysis as well as financial expenses. Subsequently, optimized GC method has provided fatty acid profile of Serbian traditional dry-fermented sausage characterized by very favorable composition, since the high content of polyunsaturated fatty acids is quite desirable from the aspect of human's health. Thus, the optimized GC method could be enforced in the study of a wide range of food samples that contain fat, raw materials used in their preparation and similar products.
