TI  - RETRACTED: Cardiovascular outcomes of ethyl eicosapentaenoic acid in diabetes mellitus: A meta-analysis (Retracted Article)
T2  - ANNALS OF MEDICINE AND SURGERY
AB  - Background: We aim to conduct a comprehens e meta-analysis encompassing all studies to assess the efficacy of Vascepa in patients with diabetes mellitus (DM in preventing or treating existing coronary artery disease (CAD). Methods: Digital databases were que ed. Odd ratios (OR) were calculated for the following outcomes: composite outcome, all-cause mor ality, and cardiovascular mortality. Results: A total of 4 rand mized co rol trials (33,092 patients; Vascepa n = 16586; Placebo n = 16506) were included in our aalysis. T e overall mean age was 64.3 years old (Vascepa = 64.3 years; Placebo = 64.3 years). The sample was 61 % mal (Vascepa = 60.8%; Placebo = 62.1%). In patients with DM, Vascepa was found to have no s gnificant effect on he primary composite outcome (OR 0.97, 95%CI 0.91-1.04, p > 0.05), all-cause mortality (R 0 6, 95%C 0.90-1.03, p > 0.05), and cardiovascular mortality (OR 0.90, 95%CI 0.74-1.10, p > 0 05). Subg up analysis by Vascepa type and treatment type was similarly non-significant. Con lusion: Our sdy concluded that Vascepa did not affect cardiovascular outcomes in patients with DM.
