TI  - Hypertriglyceridemia: what is the management?
T2  - CORRESPONDANCES EN METABOLISMES HORMONES DIABETES ET NUTRITION
AB  - Hypertriglyceridemia is a frequent dyslipidernia. It is often neglicted and poorly known. It is due to several metabolism disturbances with a great heterogeneity. It is associated a high cardiovascular risk, and, in major hypertriglyceridemia to a high risk of severe acute pancreatitis. Genetic abnormalite may play an exclusive role but there is a strong interaction with nutrition and weight. Its treatment is often difficult, we a main role of dietetic advices, particularly in the metabolism syndrome. Fibrates and statins are useful, as are omega 3 fat acids. In hyperchylomicronemia, new agents are emergercy.
